153
00:09:57,967 --> 00:10:01,319
There are multiple parallel
assembly lines running side by side.

154
00:10:01,918 --> 00:10:05,848
If one station pauses to fix a
part, the other lines keep moving.

155
00:10:06,442 --> 00:10:11,200
Once we separate our code base using
thin interface contract, we were

156
00:10:11,204 --> 00:10:16,237
able to stop running one giant,
slow builds for every pull request.

157
00:10:16,271 --> 00:10:19,686
Instead, we give every team their
own independent build pipeline.

158
00:10:20,379 --> 00:10:22,780
Let's look at the next slide
to see how the code change

159
00:10:22,791 --> 00:10:24,739
moves through this pipeline.

160
00:10:25,739 --> 00:10:29,263
Isolations, one team
failure from everyone else.

161
00:10:29,831 --> 00:10:31,116
How we can isolate it?

162
00:10:31,684 --> 00:10:37,395
else build modules, validate
gate, and contract integration.

163
00:10:37,972 --> 00:10:39,831
Look at the five step at the bottom right.

164
00:10:39,831 --> 00:10:45,626
So module, build, validate,
gate, contract integration.

165
00:10:46,737 --> 00:10:50,657
In this traditional mobile app, a single
broken import in the payment model

166
00:10:50,828 --> 00:10:52,823
stop the entire release for everyone.

167
00:10:53,152 --> 00:10:55,891
Here is how our independent
